<title>JAPAN: Mitsui Mining raises zinc price 6,000 yen.</title>
<headline>Mitsui Mining raises zinc price 6,000 yen.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui Mining and Smelting Co Ltd said on Tuesday it had raised its selling price for zinc by 6,000 yen to 218,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>A Mitsui official said the average price for this month would stand at 211,200 yen.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
</text>
